rule ticket_step v1
description "One step of a support ticket: from the stage it is in and the event that came, the next stage and what the desk does about it. Written for ritsu's tests"

enum ticket_stage = received | waiting | escalated | resolved
enum desk_event = customer_wrote | agent_answered | day_passed | customer_thanked
enum desk_reaction = nothing | remind_customer | page_manager | send_survey

inputs
  stage : ticket_stage
  event : desk_event
  days  : number  range >=0 <=30

outputs
  next_stage : ticket_stage
  reaction   : desk_reaction

table step
policy unique
| stage         | event            | days | -> next_stage | reaction        |
| resolved      | -                | -    | resolved      | nothing         |
| not: resolved | customer_thanked | -    | resolved      | send_survey     |
| not: resolved | agent_answered   | -    | waiting       | nothing         |
| not: resolved | customer_wrote   | -    | received      | nothing         |
| received      | day_passed       | -    | escalated     | page_manager    |
| escalated     | day_passed       | -    | escalated     | nothing         |
| waiting       | day_passed       | >=3  | escalated     | page_manager    |
| waiting       | day_passed       | <3   | waiting       | remind_customer |

examples
| stage    | event            | days | -> next_stage | reaction        |
| received | agent_answered   | 0    | waiting       | nothing         |
| waiting  | day_passed       | 1    | waiting       | remind_customer |
| waiting  | day_passed       | 3    | escalated     | page_manager    |
| waiting  | customer_thanked | 0    | resolved      | send_survey     |
